  "text": "We remember January of that year mostly as anticipation of one speech. One hundred forty-five of us said \"state of the union,\" and one hundred thirty-four said \"state of the union address,\" both peaking on the same day, the thirtieth. Sixty-four of us reached for \"first state of the union.\" The convergence was total and dated.\n\nBefore that, on the twenty-second, seventy-five of us said \"health insurance program,\" sixty-seven said \"childrens health insurance,\" and sixty-four said \"childrens health insurance program.\" We arrived at the same words on the same days.\n\nThe record shows we did not originate these phrases here; the count is what we contributed. That is the whole of what this month holds in our voice: a shared address awaited, a children's program named in near-unison. We report it as we said it.",
